      "writtenOn": "2023-03-30T13:44:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the generation of this indicates that we should use `TryFrom` and `TryInto` instead in this case.\n\nThe [`TryFrom` documentation](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/trait.TryFrom.html) says\n\n\u003e The `From` trait is intended for perfect conversions, so the `TryFrom` trait informs the programmer when a type conversion could go bad and lets them decide how to handle it.\n\nThis also matches how the standard library uses it: we have `From\u003ci8\u003e for i16`, but we have `TryFrom\u003ci16\u003e for i8`.\n\nI guess the most \"correct\" thing would be to generate `From` when the enum is complete and otherwise generate a `TryFrom` implementation.\n\nIt will probably be okay for callers: they should keep things as enums for most of the time and only convert to integers very rarely?",
      "revId": "2f79308445060b6d480222d8245c65de4144ecc7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
